    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d168">

                <pb facs="0299" n="237" sameAs="frus:frus1878/pg237"/>

                <head>No. 163.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Pierrepont to Mr. Evarts</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1877-10-25"><hi rendition="#italic">October</hi> 25, 1877</date>.
                        (Received November 7.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 238.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have finally concluded a trade-mark
                    convention with the Earl of Derby, excluding all the objectionable words about
                    which I wrote in my dispatch No. 191. The convention was signed in duplicate
                    yesterday at half past three o’clock at the foreign office, and I forward the
                    same herewith to-day.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.</p>
                <closer><signed>EDWARDS PIERREPONT.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
